2. Modules from RFCs published under BCP 78 (RFC 3978 / RFC 4748)
------------------------------------------------------------------

These RFCs replace the inline grant with a reference: "This document is subject
to the rights, licenses and restrictions contained in BCP 78". BCP 78 is
RFC 3978, whose §3.3(a)(E) names MIB modules explicitly and grants the right

    to extract, copy, publish, display, distribute, modify and
    incorporate into other works, for any purpose (and not limited to
    use within the IETF Standards Process) any executable code or code
    fragments that are included in any IETF Document (such as MIB and
    PIB modules)

That grant runs to ISOC and the IETF rather than directly to the public; the
downstream licence is the one the IETF Trust issues on the strength of it,
under its Legal Provisions Relating to IETF Documents
(https://trustee.ietf.org/license-info), which license Code Components — MIB
modules among them — under the Revised BSD Licence. Redistribution in source and
binary form is permitted, with no non-commercial restriction, so these files are
compatible with paid distribution.

This is the one group in this file that rests on a licence chain rather than on a
single grant appearing on the face of the document, and it is flagged as such for
review.

